  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "Today's {world} is not an easy {adjustment} for {young} {adult} .The {key} skill {set} for success is {persistence}, a characteristic that {researcher} say is {heavily} {influence} by {father}.Researchers from Brigham Young University (BYU) discovered that fathers are in a {unique} position to help their {adolescent} children learn persistence.",
      "cn": "对于 <u> 年轻人 </u> 而言， <u> 适应 </u> 当今的 <u> 世界 </u> 并不容易。取得成功的 <u> 关键 </u> 技能是 <u> 坚持不懈 </u> ，而 <u> 研究人员 </u> 表示，这一特质 <u> 在很大程度上 </u> 受到 <u> 父亲 </u> 的 <u> 影响 </u> 。杨百翰大学（BYU）的研究人员发现，父亲在帮助处于 <u> 青春期 </u> <u> 的 </u> 子女学会坚持不懈方面具有 <u> 独特的 </u> 地位。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "BYU professors Laura Padilla-Walker and Randal Day arrived at {these} findings after following 325 American families over several years.And {over} time, the persistence {gain} through fathers led to higher achievement in school.",
      "cn": "杨百翰大学教授劳拉·帕迪拉-沃克和兰道尔·戴在对325个美国家庭进行了数年的跟踪调查后得出了 <u> 这些 </u> 结论。而且 <u> 随着 </u> 时间的推移，从父亲那里 <u> 习得 </u> 的坚持不懈的品质使得孩子们在学校取得了更高的成就。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "“There are {relatively} few studies that {stress} the unique role of fathers,”Padilla-Walker said.“This research also helps to {prove} that characteristics such as persistence—which can be taught—are key to a child's {life} success.”",
      "cn": "帕迪拉-沃克说：“ <u> 强调 </u> 父亲这个独特角色的研究 <u> 相对 </u> 较少。这项研究还有助于 <u> 证明 </u> ，诸如坚持不懈这类可以教授的特质是孩子 <u> 人生 </u> 成功的关键。”"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "Researchers {determine} that dads {need} to {practice} an {authoritative} parenting {style}.Authoritative parenting is not {authoritarian}: {rigid}, demanding, or controlling.Rather, an authoritative parenting style includes some of the following characteristics: children feel warmth and {love} from their father; responsibility and the reasons {behind} rules are stressed; children are given an {appropriate} {level} of {autonomy}.",
      "cn": "研究人员 <u> 认为 </u> ，父亲 <u> 需要采取 </u> “ <u> 权威 </u> 型”的养育 <u> 方式 </u> 。权威型养育方式并非 <u> 专断 </u> 型的—— <u> 死板 </u> 、苛刻或控制欲强。相反，权威型养育方式具有以下一些特点：孩子能感受到来自父亲的温暖和 <u> 爱 </u> ；强调责任和规则 <u> 背后 </u> 的原因；给予孩子 <u> 适当程度 </u> 的 <u> 自主权 </u> 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "In the study, about 52 percent of the dads {exhibit} above-average levels of authoritative parenting.A key finding is that over time, children {raise} by an authoritative father were {significantly} more likely to develop persistence, which leads to better {outcome} in school.",
      "cn": "在这项研究中，约有52%的父亲 <u> 表现出 </u> 高于平均水平的权威型养育方式。一个重要发现是，随着时间的推移，由权威型父亲 <u> 养育 </u> 的孩子有 <u> 显著 </u> 可能会养成坚持不懈的品质，从而在学校取得更好的 <u> 成绩 </u> 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "06",
      "en": "This {particular} study {examine} 11 to 14-year-olds {live} in two-parent homes. {yet} the researchers suggest that {single} parents still may play a role in teaching the benefits of persistence, which is an {avenue} for {future} research.",
      "cn": "这项 <u> 特别的 </u> 研究 <u> 调查 </u> 的是 <u> 生活 </u> 在双亲家庭中的11至14岁的孩子。 <u> 不过 </u> ，研究人员认为， <u> 单亲 </u> 仍然可以在教授坚持不懈的好处方面发挥作用，这是 <u> 未来 </u> 研究的一个 <u> 方向 </u> 。"
    }
  ],
